The '''23 Marzo Bridge''' ({{langx|bl|Ponte 23 Marzo|4=23rd of March Bridge}}, {{IPA|bl|ˈponte `vɛnti ˈtre ˈmartso}}) is a [[W:Suspension bridge|suspension bridge]] spanning the [[Guadalquivir]] to connect the boroughs of [[Limón]] on the west (north) and [[Trinacria]] of [[Castejón]] via the island of [[La Baba]]. The northern section has a main span length of {{Convert|2090|m}}, making it the 48th [[W:List of longest suspension bridges|longest suspension bridge in the world]].

